course: dictionary
lesson: 537
title: Athletic: strong, fit and good at sport
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Athletic is an adjective, and it has two meanings. You can find out which one by reading the words around it. «Ballet has many famous male dancers, such as Rudolf Nureyev and Mikhail Baryshnikov, and it needs huge strength and athletic skill.» The clues are strength and skill. Dancers need strength, so athletic must mean strong, fit and good at sport.
explain: Athletic also has a second meaning, to do with athletics or sport. Athletic shoes are shoes for sport, and an athletic club is a club for sport. Ask yourself: is the word describing a person's body or ability, or is it describing something used for sport? That question helps you choose the right meaning.
explain: In the UK, athletics means running, jumping and throwing events. So an athlete is someone who takes part in these events, and athletic is the word that describes that kind of strength and skill.
fact: Athletic means strong, fit and good at sport.
fact: Athletic can also mean to do with athletics or sport, as in athletic shoes or an athletic club.
fact: In the UK, athletics means running, jumping and throwing events.
fact: Athletic build means a strong, fit body, and athletic ability means skill at sport.
fact: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «It needs huge strength and strong, fit skill» still makes sense, so you chose well.
exercise: «Ballet needs huge strength and athletic skill.» What does athletic mean here? | Slow and careful | Very old | *Strong, fit and good at sport | Quiet and calm
exercise: In the UK, what does athletics mean? | Painting pictures and drawing maps | Cooking dinner for a big family | Reading and writing stories | *Running, jumping and throwing events
exercise: Which phrase uses athletic to mean to do with sport? | *athletic shoes | a sleepy cat | a quiet library | a rainy picnic
test: Mia has an athletic build. What does this tell you about Mia? | She is lost in the woods | *She is strong and fit | She is sleepy and tired | She is very old
test: Which word is closest in meaning to athletic? | Curt | Glum | Barely | *Fit
exam: Read: «Her athletic ability won the race.» What does athletic mean here? | Lost in the rain | Dinner at seven | *Good at sport and strong | Very quiet and shy
